@startuml logical-view
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title AISafe - Logical view (UML components, level 1)

skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 16

actor "Client" as client

interface "Auth API" as authApi
interface "Flights API" as foApi
interface "Airports & Routes API" as arApi
interface "Aircraft & Maintenance API" as amApi

component "login" as login
component "flight-ops" as fo
component "airports-routes" as ar
component "aircraft-maintenance" as am

interface "Routes internal\n(C2, C5)" as arInternal
interface "Aircraft internal\n(C1, C3, C4)" as amInternal

client ..> authApi
client ..> foApi
client ..> arApi
client ..> amApi

authApi -- login
foApi -- fo
arApi -- ar
amApi -- am

fo ..> arInternal
fo ..> amInternal
ar ..> amInternal
arInternal -- ar
amInternal -- am

note as contracts
  <b>Provided interfaces</b>
  Auth API: /api/auth
  Flights API: /api/flights
  Airports & Routes API: /api/airports, /api/routes, /api/network
  Aircraft & Maintenance API: /api/aircrafts, /api/aircraftModels, /api/maintenance
  Routes internal: C2 GET /internal/routes/{o}/{d}, C5 PUT /internal/flights/{id}
  Aircraft internal: C1 GET /internal/aircrafts/{reg},
    C3 GET /internal/aircraft-models/{name}, C4 PUT /internal/flights/{id}

  <b>Every component</b> runs as 3 equal replicas, each with its own database,
  which also offer and require /internal/replicas/** among themselves
  (forwarding, replication, sync). Dependencies between services go one way:
  flight-ops -> airports-routes -> aircraft-maintenance. Nobody calls login:
  the services check the JWT themselves.
end note
@enduml
